1858
02:00:10,327 --> 02:00:12,110
Bro, raw ka scene lagta hai yeh.

1859
02:00:12,610 --> 02:00:14,093
Yeah, ISI, you never know.

1860
02:00:14,173 --> 02:00:19,295
Because of his father's postings, he's lived all over India and speaks excellent Hindi.

1861
02:00:19,375 --> 02:00:25,234
In fact, he's more similar to North Indians and South Indians in many ways, except food.

1862
02:00:25,314 --> 02:00:30,127
It feels like he has the best of both worlds and that makes makes him such an open,

1863
02:00:30,207 --> 02:00:31,895
grounded and empathetic person.

1864
02:00:31,975 --> 02:00:37,829
And now the question we asked in the beginning about Desis who were brought abroad,

1865
02:00:37,909 --> 02:00:39,300
I also mentioned this in that.

1866
02:00:39,380 --> 02:00:44,340
I also said that different cultures and interactions change your perspective in life.

1867
02:00:44,420 --> 02:00:45,340
And you're more grounded.

1868
02:00:45,420 --> 02:00:48,820
And the same thing applies to this because he was moving.

1869
02:00:49,140 --> 02:00:49,690
across India.

1870
02:00:49,770 --> 02:00:52,338
Being with him has completely shifted my perspective.

1871
02:00:52,418 --> 02:00:58,940
I've always seen myself as a fairly rational person with a worldview shaped by questioning rather than accepting things blindly.

1872
02:00:59,080 --> 02:01:01,742
But hearing his stories about India, his religion,

1873
02:01:01,822 --> 02:01:07,026
and his way of seeing the world made me realize how much of what I grew up with was filtered and one-sided.

1874
02:01:07,106 --> 02:01:10,971
I honestly feel like I grew up in a kind of a controlled and narrative,

1875
02:01:11,051 --> 02:01:13,190
a curated version of truth.

1876
02:01:13,270 --> 02:01:16,016
Almost every time we meet Pakistani students here,

1877
02:01:16,096 --> 02:01:19,481
their first question to my boyfriend is, are you Muslim?

1878
02:01:19,561 --> 02:01:23,213
It's like his entire identity gets reduced to that single question.

1879
02:01:23,293 --> 02:01:27,778
I'm not someone who lets one incident define an entire community,

1880
02:01:27,858 --> 02:01:31,710
but it's happened so many times that I can't help but notice the pattern.

1881
02:01:31,790 --> 02:01:36,747
It's disheartening because I thought Pakistanis abroad, especially the younger generation,

1882
02:01:36,827 --> 02:01:40,593
would be more open-minded, more curious about people as individuals,

1883
02:01:40,673 --> 02:01:42,110
not as products of religion.

1884
02:01:42,190 --> 02:01:46,995
I don't understand why this question is asked.

1885
02:01:47,075 --> 02:01:49,830
Why is that question even relevant?

1886
02:01:49,910 --> 02:01:54,670
I mean, if you are meeting someone, why are you asking their religion?

1887
02:01:54,750 --> 02:01:59,510
Which reminds me, I went to a place for dinner. I was meeting this.

1888
02:01:59,590 --> 02:02:01,510
meeting this family for the first time.

1889
02:02:01,590 --> 02:02:07,510
So, during that time, there was a Friday holiday.

1890
02:02:07,590 --> 02:02:09,510
Okay? So I went to their house.

1891
02:02:09,590 --> 02:02:16,510
They asked me, so how was your day? So I said, yeah, it was good. I went for Namaz. This, that.

1892
02:02:16,590 --> 02:02:19,510
But I was telling them how my day was, what did I do.

1893
02:02:19,590 --> 02:02:22,510
So they asked, are you a Muslim?

1894
02:02:22,590 --> 02:02:25,590
Okay, seemingly, they were also Muslims.

1895
02:02:25,830 --> 02:02:27,750
I mean, their names are all there, everything.

1896
02:02:27,830 --> 02:02:34,636
So I said, yes, but like, not as much practicing as it should be, but yeah,

1897
02:02:34,716 --> 02:02:36,750
I do my Jummas and everything.

1898
02:02:36,830 --> 02:02:43,750
He said, okay, we are atheists. And I'm like, okay, fine. I mean, like, why is that the first thing I'm hearing about it?

1899
02:02:43,830 --> 02:02:48,374
Some people are there, they are there, so like this is the same thing, that H.S.

1900
02:02:48,454 --> 02:02:52,830
Onian, until he tells that he has gone to study, the conversation does not start.

1901
02:02:52,910 --> 02:02:54,390
This is the same thing with Lums.

1902
02:02:54,470 --> 02:02:57,630
So this is the same thing with atheists in Pakistan at least.

1903
02:02:57,710 --> 02:02:59,630
They say, just know.

1904
02:02:59,710 --> 02:03:01,630
It's like a vegan.

1905
02:03:01,710 --> 02:03:04,310
How do you know when a vegan walks into a room?

1906
02:03:04,390 --> 02:03:06,990
You don't have to know because they'll tell themselves.

1907
02:03:07,070 --> 02:03:12,790
So I said, okay, as long as it works for you.

1908
02:03:12,870 --> 02:03:16,790
What should I do with this knowledge? Who you practice?

1909
02:03:16,870 --> 02:03:20,870
So I don't understand this thing. How do you meet someone for the first time and ask about their…

1910
02:03:21,010 --> 02:03:22,945
about their religion or their faith.

1911
02:03:23,025 --> 02:03:25,223
I have Christian friends.

1912
02:03:25,303 --> 02:03:28,349
I don't even know if they are Catholic or Protestant.

1913
02:03:28,429 --> 02:03:29,660
Because it's personal.

1914
02:03:29,740 --> 02:03:30,444
What can I do?

1915
02:03:30,524 --> 02:03:31,643
He is a good person.

1916
02:03:31,723 --> 02:03:33,726
Does he give me respect?

1917
02:03:33,806 --> 02:03:36,740
He or she gives me respect and kindness and caring.

1918
02:03:36,820 --> 02:03:38,163
That's all that matters.

1919
02:03:38,243 --> 02:03:40,034
Whatever he does, what can I do?

1920
02:03:40,114 --> 02:03:45,236
Recently we sublet our apartment to a Pakistani girl around our age from Karachi.

1921
02:03:45,316 --> 02:03:46,827
Very modern on the surface.

1922
02:03:46,907 --> 02:03:48,290
Yet the first thing she asked

1923
02:03:48,370 --> 02:03:53,730
asked my boyfriend was again, are you Muslim? He just said he was a Buddhist, as if that would

1924
02:03:54,050 --> 02:03:54,550
make things easier and then went on to assure her that we only eat halal meat. It was both

1925
02:03:58,930 --> 02:03:59,430
funny and sad at the same time. And let me tell you, this is not an isolated incident. Another

1926
02:04:09,970 --> 02:04:15,080
girl just backed out of the sublet when she found out that my boyfriend was a Hindu. I'm just disappointed. I expected more, more depth, more compassion, more rationality from Pakistanis living abroad. But.

1927
02:04:15,160 --> 02:04:22,080
But the thing is, this living abroad product is from here and it has gone from here.

1928
02:04:22,160 --> 02:04:28,080
So you can't expect, just because global positioning changes more than ours.

1929
02:04:28,160 --> 02:04:35,080
Our parameter doesn't change and it doesn't change for a long time.

1930
02:04:35,160 --> 02:04:41,160
So you can expect that kind of openness from those who are brought up there.

1931
02:04:42,200 --> 02:04:44,120
I have interacted with different cultures throughout my life.

1932
02:04:44,200 --> 02:04:48,120
Here, I don't make friends outside of Sunni.

1933
02:04:48,200 --> 02:04:52,120
I am not speaking for all.

1934
02:04:52,200 --> 02:04:55,120
But it happens, don't sit in Shia.

1935
02:04:55,200 --> 02:04:58,120
Don't get away from religion, etc.

1936
02:04:58,200 --> 02:05:00,120
We don't get away from our sect.

1937
02:05:00,200 --> 02:05:02,120
So religion is a very far thing.

1938
02:05:02,200 --> 02:05:04,120
And all those who are listening, how many Hindu friends do you have?

1939
02:05:04,200 --> 02:05:08,120
If you live in Pakistan, if you live in Karachi, then the Hindu population is more here.

1940
02:05:08,200 --> 02:05:09,440
It's more in Sindh overall.

1941
02:05:09,600 --> 02:05:12,400
So how many of your friends are not of your religion?

1942
02:05:13,400 --> 02:05:14,400
Very few.

1943
02:05:14,880 --> 02:05:18,600
So, the product is from here, right?

1944
02:05:18,680 --> 02:05:28,120
Just because of that, in Stuttgart or Dresden or Dusseldorf, makes them less Pakistani.

1945
02:05:28,200 --> 02:05:30,240
They're just that same Pakistani.

1946
02:05:30,320 --> 02:05:34,320
Anyway, it feels like no matter how far we go, we carry the same narrow lenses with us.

1947
02:05:34,400 --> 02:05:35,280
What kind of surprise?

1948
02:05:35,360 --> 02:05:41,697
What surprised me was learning from my boyfriend how relatively peacefully Muslims,

1949
02:05:41,777 --> 02:05:44,880
Hindus and Christians coexist in South India.

1950
02:05:45,160 --> 02:05:48,080
That's because they have a shared culture.

1951
02:05:48,160 --> 02:05:50,080
They have seen each other.

1952
02:05:50,160 --> 02:05:56,080
When you get up together, then the differences are less. Similarities are more.

1953
02:05:56,160 --> 02:05:59,080
This is the issue of Indians and Pakistan.

1954
02:05:59,160 --> 02:06:03,160
Now we are being taught controlled narrative here and there.

1955
02:06:03,680 --> 02:06:09,960
When we sit together in a Dubai restaurant, they say, there are more similarities than differences.

1956
02:06:10,040 --> 02:06:11,400
So let's focus on that.

1957
02:06:11,480 --> 02:06:17,388
But since there is no interaction here, now there in the South, as you are saying,

1958
02:06:17,468 --> 02:06:18,600
there is not much.

1959
02:06:18,680 --> 02:06:24,840
That's because Muslims are selling crackers for Diwali, they are also selling colors for Holi.

1960
02:06:24,920 --> 02:06:26,360
They don't think like this.

1961
02:06:26,440 --> 02:06:27,480
Business is business.

1962
02:06:27,560 --> 02:06:31,860
That's why from his perspective, the idea of asking someone's religion right after meeting.

1963
02:06:31,940 --> 02:06:33,486
meeting them is just absurd.

1964
02:06:33,566 --> 02:06:36,761
He has told me that this almost never happens in India.

1965
02:06:36,841 --> 02:06:40,998
I don't know if this is a question or more of an emotional dump,

1966
02:06:41,078 --> 02:06:47,855
but I guess what I'm really wondering is why do we as a community struggle so much to see beyond religion?

1967
02:06:47,935 --> 02:06:53,592
How do we unlearn this reflex to define people by faith before we even know who they really are?

1968
02:06:53,672 --> 02:06:58,573
Why is our generation, even after getting international exposure and living abroad,

1969
02:06:58,653 --> 02:06:59,320
still so stuck on

1970
02:06:59,400 --> 02:07:02,120
on this superficial judgmental mentality.

1971
02:07:02,800 --> 02:07:08,200
Uh, P.S. I was one of those people who got inspired by your study in Germany video.

1972
02:07:08,280 --> 02:07:10,720
It literally played a part in me ending up here.

1973
02:07:11,240 --> 02:07:15,600
Been a fan ever since and I've successfully converted my boyfriend into one as well.

1974
02:07:16,480 --> 02:07:19,840
Okay, I made him a fan. I thought conversion. You didn't make me a conversion.

1975
02:07:20,280 --> 02:07:21,600
Anyway, to each their own.

1976
02:07:22,480 --> 02:07:27,110
So yeah, oh, that's good to hear. So I, for those who don't know, when I went to Germany for the first time in 2017,

1977
02:07:27,190 --> 02:07:29,110
I went to Germany for the first time. I met two students.

1978
02:07:29,190 --> 02:07:33,110
Adnan and I forgot the other one's name.

1979
